**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFileJsonTests`

**How to implement.** The `.kit-json` text: canonical JSON, validated against its own schema on read, a version mismatch a typed error (001 §B 'No up-converters … The same holds for kit files'; the S4.1 brief: kit.schema.json is validated on read; .spec-md §4 'Stored formats', §6 'JSON + schema'). It reuses the stack of steps 27-31, and the two bodies a second format would copy move to one home each. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs`. (a) `type JsonNode with member this.canonicalFileText : string` is the indented canonical rendering (step 27) followed by one `\n`: the form of every file the app writes. `LibraryEntryEnvelope.fileText` (step 30) and `CatalogueManifest.fileText` (step 31), in `EntryFileJson.fs`, now render through it, and the code that appended the `\n` in each is deleted. (b) `parseVersionedText<'Value> (validate : JsonElement -> Result<unit, StorageError>) (extension : FileExtension) (expected : FileSchemaVersion) (text : string) : Result<'Value, StorageError>` holds the read order of `LibraryFileText.parseCatalogueManifest` (step 31), moved: parse the text (`MalformedJsonErr`); `validate` the root element (`SchemaValidationErr`); compare its top-level `schemaVersion` with `expected` before anything binds (`UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` of `{ fileExtension = extension; found; expected }`, step 30); bind through `options` (`MalformedJsonErr`). Every throwing .NET call is caught there. It is marked `[<ElevationBoundary(nameof StorageBoundary, "a versioned file's text, parsed, validated and bound at the storage seam (spec 0050 S4.1)")>]`, because its signature carries the text. `parseCatalogueManifest` now calls it with `SchemaValidation.validateCatalogueManifest`, `CatalogueManifest.extension` and `CatalogueManifest.currentSchemaVersion`, and its own body is deleted, so step 31's facts stay green unchanged. (2) The schema. New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/kit.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 like `schema/library-catalogue.schema.json` (step 31), with `$id` `https://berreman/schema/kit.json`. `schemaVersion` is a positive integer, checked unconditionally. Only under `if` it is 1 (`then`): every key of `KitFile` is present (`schemaVersion`, `id`, `name`, `author`, `created`, `modified`, `notes`, `sendExclude`) and no other (`additionalProperties: false`); `id` is the GUID string of `library-common.schema.json` (step 30), referenced by its `$id`; `name` is a string holding a non-white-space character (the pattern `\S`); `author` and `notes` are strings; `created` and `modified` are strings; and `sendExclude` is an array of non-empty strings. A file of another version therefore passes the schema and reaches the typed version check. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside step 30's `schema/library-*.schema.json` items of `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateKitFile (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith` (step 29), its schema loaded once behind a `lazy` that loads the common schema first, as step 30's entry schemas do (`SchemaValidation.fs:17-21`: `JsonSchema.FromText` registers an `$id` only once). (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs`, `module KitFolderStore` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `CatalogueImportStore.fs` (step 94): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. It opens `OpticalConstructor.Domain.Kit`. (a) `type KitFile with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` is `nodeOf this` (step 27) rendered by `canonicalFileText`, so a kit file is indented canonical JSON with sorted keys, LF line ends and one final `\n`. The two instants are written by the serializer's own ISO 8601 form, which keeps every tick and the `Z` of a UTC instant. (b) `type KitFileText with member this.parseKitFile : Result<KitFile, StorageError>` is `parseVersionedText validateKitFile KitFile.extension KitFile.currentSchemaVersion this.value`. There are no up-converters and no fallback readers. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFileJsonTests.fs`, `module KitFileJsonTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its kit file is `KitFile.create` over `KitId (Guid.Parse "6f1c2a9e-3b7d-4e25-9a41-0c8d5e7f2b16")`, the name `Optics: QZ/LR — µ` and `KitAuthor "Test author"`, with `created` at `ClockTime` of `DateTime(2026, 11, 3, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc).AddTicks 1234567L` and `modified` one day later, the notes `Two lines\nof notes` and the globs `**/*.dng` and `data/raw/big/**`. `a kit file round-trips through its canonical text`: `fileText` then `parseKitFile` answers an equal kit file; the text holds no `\r`, ends with exactly one `\n`, lists its top-level keys in ordinal order (`author`, `created`, `id`, `modified`, `name`, `notes`, `schemaVersion`, `sendExclude`), keeps `µ` and `—` unescaped, and writes `created` as `2026-11-03T12:00:00.1234567Z`; writing the parsed kit file again gives the same text. `a kit file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: the text with `schemaVersion` set to 2, both with its body intact and as `{ "schemaVersion": 2 }` alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = KitFile.extension`, `found = FileSchemaVersion 2` and `expected = FileSchemaVersion 1`. `a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds`: the text without `name`, with an extra key `colour`, with `name` set to `"   "`, and with `id` set to `not-a-guid`, each answer `SchemaValidationErr` with messages; the text `{` answers `MalformedJsonErr`.

**Acceptance.** After the kit file's text lands, `KitFileText.parseKitFile` MUST validate against `schema/kit.schema.json` and refuse another schema version with `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, and the entry, manifest and kit file texts MUST render through `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a kit file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds`, the count rising by 3, with every `EntryFileJsonTests` fact (steps 30-31) passing as written; and build, elevation and the eleven s15 invariants MUST pass.
